hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4456","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uqaym said: “A letter from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was read to us from the land of Juhayna, while I was a young boy: That you should not benefit from “The death is due to something with no skin or nerve.”"
"4457","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Uqaym said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wrote to us: Not to enjoy the dead body without any skin or skin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4458","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Hilal al-Wazzan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uqaym, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote Peace and blessings of God be upon him, to Juhayna that you should not enjoy the dead body without any skin or nerve.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The most correct opinion on this topic is in The skins of dead bodies when tanned, the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maimuna, and God Almighty I know"
"4459","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Bishr bin Omar informed us, he said: Malik told us. H and Al-Harith bin Miskin, I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded that The skins of dead animals can be enjoyed if they are tanned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4460","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abi Orouba, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, “The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he forbade the skins of wild beasts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4461","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade silk, gold, and tiger tracks.”"
"4462","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiyah told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, he said: The delegation of Al-Miqdam bin Ma’di was preparing for Muawiyah, He said to him: “I adjure you by God. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing the skins of wild beasts and riding on them? He said: Yes.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The most authentic thing on this topic is the skins of dead bodies if they have been tanned, the hadith of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah Ibn Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas"
"4463","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd By God, he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of the conquest, while he was in Mecca, saying: “Indeed, God Almighty and His Messenger forbade the sale of alcohol. And the dead carcasses, and the pigs, and the idols. It was said: O Messenger of God, have you seen the fat of the dead carcasses? For ships are coated with it, and ships are greased with it. Skins, and people use them in the morning. He said: No, it is forbidden. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said at that: God fought the Jews. When God Almighty forbade fat for them, they packed it, then sold it and consumed its price.”"
"4464","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Umar was informed that Samra sold wine and said: May God fight Samra. Did he not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God fight the Jews? It was forbidden to them. The fat and beautify it.” Sufyan said: He means they melted it"
"4465","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maimuna “A mouse fell into ghee and died, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked and said: Throw it and what is around it and eat it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4466","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi informed us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maymunah, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a mouse that fell into Solid ghee, and he said: Take it and what is around it and throw it away. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4467","Khushish bin Asram told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Budhawih informed me, that Muammar mentioned it, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maymunah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He was asked about The mouse fell into the ghee, and he said: If it is solid, throw it away, and whatever is around it, but if it is liquid, do not bring it near it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4468","Salama bin Ahmad bin Sulaym bin Othman Al-Fawzi told us, he said: Grandfather Al-Khattab, meaning Ibn Othman, told us, he said: Muhammad bin Himyar told us. He said: Thabit bin Ajlan told us, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He passed by a dead goat and said: It would not be the case for the people of this sheep if they benefited from its skin. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4469","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, he said: Saeed bin Khaled told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a fly lands in one of you’s vessel, let him remove it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4470","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran Al-Basri informed us, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, informed us, he said: I read to Abdul Hamid Bin Jafar, my father told me, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Usayd bin Zuhair, on the authority of his father Usayd bin Zuhair, “He went out to his people to Banu Haritha. He said: O Banu Haritha, a calamity has befallen you. They said: What is it? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. Renting the land. We said: O Messenger of God, then we would rent it for some kind of love. He said: No. He said: And we would rent it for figs. He said: No, and we would rent it for figs. Because of the watering spring, he said: “Plant it or give it to your brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4471","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya told us, and he is the son of Adam, he said: Mufaddal told us, and he is Ibn Muhalhalil, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Usayd ibn Zuhair, who said: Rafi’ ibn Khadij came to us and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade you.” On behalf of the field, and the field is a third and a quarter, and on behalf of the Muzabanah, and the Muzabanah purchases what is on the tops of palm trees for such-and-such an wasq of dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4472","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, I heard Mujahid, speaking on the authority of Usayd bin Zuhair. He said: Rafi’ bin Khadij came to us and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us, and obedience to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. It is better for you. He forbade you from farming, and said: Whoever has land, let him give it to you, or let him leave it, and he forbade squatting, And the Muzabanah, a man has a great deal of money from palm trees, and the man comes and takes it with so-and-so and such-and-such an wasq of dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4473","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Usayd bin Zuhair, he said: Rafi’ bin Khadij, and he said: I did not understand, so he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade you from a matter that would benefit you, and obedience to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. It is better for you than what benefits you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade you regarding the field, and the field that is cultivated is a third. And a quarter, so whoever has land and does not need it, let him give it to his brother or leave it, and he forbade you from squabbling, and the squatter, the man. He comes to a lot of palm trees with a lot of money and says: Get him such-and-such and such-and-such an wasq of dates that year.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4474","Ishaq bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq told me, he said: Affan told us, he said: Abdul Wahid told us, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, On the authority of Mujahid, he said: Usayd, my nephew Rafi’ bin Khadij, told me: Rafi’ bin Khadij said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade A matter that was beneficial to us, and obedience to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is more beneficial to us. He said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it, and if he is unable from it, let his brother cultivate it.”"
"4475","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr, informed us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I took a peacock in the hand until I brought it to Ibn Rafi’ bin Khadij, and he told him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He forbade renting land.” Abu Tawus refused, and said: I heard Ibn Abbas, who does not see anything wrong with that. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Abu Awanah, on the authority of Abu Husayn. On the authority of Mujahid, he said: He said: On the authority of Rafi’, mursal."
"4476","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Rafi’ bin Khadij said: “He forbade us.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of a matter that was beneficial to us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded the head and the eye. He forbade us from We accept the land with some of its taxes.”"
"4477","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by the land of a man from the Ansar who was known to be in need, and he said: Whose land is this? He said: To so-and-so. He gave it to me with a reward, and said: If he had given it to his brother, then Rafi’ al-Ansar came and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade you from “A matter that was kind to you, and obedience to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is more beneficial to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4478","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the field.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4479","4482 Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, who said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Rafi’ ibn Khadij narrated, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us and forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us. He said: Who would do it for us?” land, let him cultivate it, or give it to his brother, or scatter it.”"
"4480","Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Shu`bah told me, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata and a peacock, And Mujahid, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us and forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us, and commanded The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is better for us. He said: “Whoever has land, let him cultivate it, or leave it, or let him give it away,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: What indicates that Tawus did not hear this hadith from Rafi’ ibn Khadij is that"
"4481","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Zakaria bin Adiy told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: It was Tawus hates to rent out his land for gold and silver, and he does not see any harm in a third or a quarter, so Mujahid said to him: Go to Ibn Rafi’ bin Khadij, so listen to his hadith. He said: By God, if I had known that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had forbidden what I did, But someone more knowledgeable than him, Ibn Abbas, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only said: “For one of you to give his brother his land.” Better than taking a known tax on her.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: There was a disagreement over Ata’ in this hadith, so he said: Abd al-Malik. Ibn Maysarah, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, and we mentioned him before and said: Abd al-Malik Ibn Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of A tyrant (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4482","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever has land, let him cultivate it. If he is unable to cultivate it, let him give it to his Muslim brother, and not He cultivates it.”"
"4483","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or give it to his brother, and not force it.”"
"4484","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hamza, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “There were people who were virtuous. Two lands that they owned by half, a third, and a quarter, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or “He plants it or he keeps it.”"
"4485","Issa bin Muhammad, who is Abu Umair bin Al-Nahhas, told us, and Issa bin Yunus, who is Al-Fakhouri, said: Damra told us, on the authority of Ibn Shudhab, on the authority of Matar bin Tahman, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us, and he said: “Who was she?” He has land, so let him cultivate it or cultivate it, but not rent it out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4486","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who narrated it: “He forbade \about renting the land\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4487","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, and Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, forbade conspiring with one another, trading with one another, competing with one another, and selling fruit to the point of feeding anyone but the naked. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4488","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ata On the authority of Jabir, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade muqāṭāliḥa, muzabānah, communicating with one another, and the two of them unless it is known,” he said. Abu Abd al-Rahman: And in the narration of Hammam bin Yahya, there is evidence that Ata’ did not hear his hadith from Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4489","Ahmad bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Hammam bin Yahya told us, he said: Ata asked Sulayman bin Musa, he said: It happened Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or let his brother cultivate it, and not force it.” His brother,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The prohibition of quarreling was narrated by Yazid ibn Nu’aym, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"4490","Muhammad bin Idris told us, he said: Abu Tawba told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Nu`aym, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the field, which is the farmstead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4491","Al-Thiqah told us, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade pacts, rivalry, conversing, and communication. He said: “Contacting is selling the fruit before it blossoms, and conversing is selling the vineyard for such-and-such for a Saa’.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4492","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the practice of rivalry and competition.”"
"4493","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya told us, and he is the son of Adam, he said: Abdul Rahim, who is the son of Suleiman, told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade rivalry. “And the Muzabanah” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4494","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yazid bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Hamran told us, he said: Abdullah bin Hamran told us Al-Hamid bin Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “On the authority of Al-Muhahaqilah and Al-Muzabanah.” This hadith was narrated by Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4495","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, he said: Othman bin Murrah told us, he said: I asked Al-Qasim about farming, and he talked about Rafi’ bin Khadij, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the practice of competition and competition.”"
"4496","Amr bin Ali told us again, he said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Murrah, he said: I asked Al-Qasim about renting the land, and he said: He said Rafi’ bin Khadij: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting land.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: There was disagreement over Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab regarding it."
"4497","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Khutami, whose name is Umair ibn Yazid, he said: My uncle sent me and a servant of his. I went to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and asked him about farming. He said: Ibn Umar did not see anything wrong with it, until he reported a hadith to him on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij. So he met him, and Rafi’ said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Banu Haritha and saw crops, and said: How beautiful is the planting of Dhuhayr, and they said: Not For Dhuhair. He said: Isn’t it the land of Dhuhair? They said: Yes, but he planted it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take your crops and return them. To him I spent his money. He said: So we took our crops and returned to him his money. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4498","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade muhaqalātāḥ and trading, and said: Only three things are cultivated: a man who has land, so he cultivates it; Or a man who was granted land and he cultivates what he was given, or a man who leased land for gold or silver.”"
"4499","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Saeed, he said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Muqāliḥa,” Sa`id said: And he mentioned something similar. Narrated by Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Tariq"
"4500","Al-Harith bin Miskin said: I read it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id bin Al-Musayyib, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the practice of competition and competition.”"
"4501","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My uncle told me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ikrimah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd Al-Rahman bin Labiba, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas, said: “The farm owners used to work as farmers in the time of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, their farms and the crops that the waterer should have, so they came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and they disputed over some of that. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade them from doing so, saying: “Do it with gold and silver.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4502","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Hakim, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, On the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: “We used to squat with the land during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we would rent it for a third, a quarter, and food.” Namely, one day a man from my cousins came and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me about a matter that was beneficial to us, and I voluntarily God and His Messenger are more beneficial to us. He forbade us from occupying the land, and forcing it to eat a third, a quarter, or the specified food, and the Lord of the Earth commanded that He cultivates it or cultivates it, and he hates renting it, and anything else.”"
"4503","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Ya’la bin Hakim wrote to me, Indeed, I heard Suleiman bin Yasar, speaking, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, who said: “We used to divide the land, plotting it for a third, a quarter, and the designated food.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4504","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ya’la bin Hakim, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, that Rafi’ bin Khadij said: “We were arguing during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he claimed that some of his cousins had come to him, so he said: The Messenger of God forbade me.” God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a matter that was beneficial to us, and obedience to God and His Messenger is more beneficial to us. We said: What is that? He said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or let his brother cultivate it, and he should not rent it out for a third, a quarter, or specified food.”"
"4505","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Hujain bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Abi Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Hanzala bin Qais, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, said: My uncle told me, “They used to colonize the land during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, including what grows on Wednesdays, and some of the crops that the owner of the land excludes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from “That,” so I said to Rafi’: How did he rent it for dinars and dirhams? Rafi’ said: There is no problem with dinars and dirhams. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4506","Al-Mughirah bin Abdul-Rahman told me, he said: Isa told us, he is Ibn Yunus, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Abi Abd. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Qais Al-Ansari, said: I asked Rafi’ bin Khadij, “about renting land for gold or paper,” and he said, “There is no problem.” Thus, during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, people only rented out what was on the troughs and the sides of the tables, so this was accepted. And this one will perish, and this one will be spared, and that one will perish, and the people had no rent except this one, and for that reason he was forbidden from him. As for something known, Guaranteed, there is nothing wrong with it.”"
"4507","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Qais, that he asked Rafi’ bin Khadij asked about leasing land, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade leasing land. I said: for gold and paper? He said: As for With gold and paper, there is no harm in it.”"
"4508","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Qais, he said: I asked Rafi’ bin Khadij Regarding renting land, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting land. I said: for gold and silver? He said: No, he only forbade it.” From it with what comes out of it, but as for gold and silver, there is no problem.”"
"4509","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Waki’, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Qais said: I asked Rafi’ bin Khadij about renting white land for gold and silver, and he said: It is permissible and there is no problem with it. That is an obligation. \Earth\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4510","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us in his hadith, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Qais, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from renting our land, and there was no gold or silver on that day, so there was The man rents his land with what is in the spring, and known things"
"4511","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah informed us, saying: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma’ told us, on the authority of Juwayriyah, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Salem bin Abdullah told him and asked him about renting farms, and he said: Rafi’ bin Khadij told us that his two uncles and they were They witnessed Badr and told them, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the rental of farms.” So Abdullah left and hated it, and was He forced her before that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4512","Abd Al-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Aqeel bin Khaled told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Salem bin Abdullah told me that Abdullah bin Omar was plotting his land until he heard that Rafi’ bin Khadij was forbidding About renting land. Abdullah met him and said: O Ibn Khadij, what do you talk about from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about renting land? Rafi’ said to Abdullah: I heard my uncle, who had witnessed Badr, telling the people of the house that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Regarding leasing the land, Abdullah said: I knew during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the land would be rented. Then Abdullah feared That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did something about that that he did not know, so he left the land lease."
"4513","Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili told me, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: We were informed that Rafi’ bin Khadij He used to say that he heard his two blind men, and they had allegedly witnessed Badr, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade leasing land.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4514","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shuaib, Al-Zuhri said: It was Ibn Al-Musayyab, saying: “ There is nothing wrong with expropriating land for gold and paper, and Rafi’ bin Khadij used to narrate that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade \that\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4515","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Abu Khuzaymah Abdullah bin Tarif told me, on the authority of Abdul Al-Karim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Rafi’ bin Khadij said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting land,” he said. Ibn Shihab: Rafi’ was asked after that how they used to cultivate the land. He said: With some specific food, and it is stipulated that we have something that grows ears. The earth, and the faces of the streams"
"4516","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Fudayl told us, he said: Musa, who is Ibn Uqba, told us, he said: Nafi’ told me, Rafi’ bin Khadij told Abdullah bin Omar that his cousins came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then they returned to Rafi’. They were informed, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting farms.” Abdullah said: We knew that he was the owner of A farm that he owned during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the condition that he would have access to the watering spring from which water gushes, and a group of I don't know how much hay it is? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4517","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Ibn Aoun informed us, on the authority of Nafi’, Ibn Umar used to take Renting the land. A hadith reached him on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij. So he took my hand and walked to Rafi’ and I was with him. Rafi’ told him, on the authority of some His general statement, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting land,” so Abdullah left after (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4518","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He was renting the land, until Rafi’ told him, on the authority of some of his relatives, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting The land” and he left it afterward (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4519","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar was He cultivated his farms until he heard, at the end of the caliphate of Muawiyah, that Rafi’ ibn Khadij reported therein a prohibition on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he came to him and I was with him and asked him, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting farms.” So Ibn Umar left it after And when he was asked about it, he said: Rafi’ bin Khadij claimed that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4520","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam ibn Ayan told me, saying: Shuaib ibn al-Layth told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Kathir ibn It was reported, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah bin Omar used to rent farms, so it was narrated that “Rafi’ bin Khadij is preferred on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He acknowledged that he forbade that. Nafi’ said: So he went out to him at the court and I was with him. He asked him, and he said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. “peace and blessings of God be upon him” about renting farms, so Abdullah abandoned them."
"4521","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, that a man Ibn Omar was informed that Rafi’ ibn Khadij was recently interested in renting land, so I and the man who told him went off with him until he came to Rafi’. Rafi’ told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting land.” So Abdullah abandoned renting the land."
"4522","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Juwayriyah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, that Rafi’ bin Khadij Abdullah bin Omar narrated, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade renting farms.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4523","Hisham bin Ammar told us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us and mentioned a word that means it, he said: Hafs bin told me Anan, on the authority of Nafi’, that he narrated to him, saying: “Ibn Umar was plotting his land with some of what he produced from it, and he was informed that Rafi’ ibn Khadij, He discourages that, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade that. He said: We used to cover the earth before we knew Rafi’. Then he found it within himself, so he placed his hand on my shoulders until we were pushed to Rafi’, and Abdullah said to him: Did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He forbade renting land. Rafi’ said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Do not rent land for anything. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4524","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad and Nafi’, who said: I am Rafi’ bin Khadij, “that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade leasing land.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Ibn Umar, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, and there was disagreement over Amr bin Dinar, in his narration on the authority of (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4525","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar says: We used to tell people and did not see any harm in that, until Rafi’ bin Khadij claimed, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade \intelligence\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4526","And Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Juraij said: I heard Amr bin Dinar, saying: I bear witness that I heard Ibn Omar, when he was asking about the news, said: “We did not see anything wrong with that until Ibn Khadij informed us in the year of the first year that he heard the Prophet praying.” May God bless him and grant him peace. “He forbids news” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4527","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: “We used not to see “The news was so bad that it was the year of the first, and Rafi’ claimed that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had forbidden it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4528","Harami bin Yunus told us, he said: A`rim told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He forbade renting land.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4529","Muhammad bin Amir told me, he said: Surayj told us, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God forbade me God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of communicating with each other, competing with one another, and competing with one another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4530","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, saying: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, and Jabir “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of fruit until it appears to be in good condition, and he forbade informing people about renting land for a third or a quarter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4531","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Tabarani told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Bahr told us, he said: Mubarak bin Saeed told us, he said: he told us Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: Abu Al-Najashi told me, he said: Rafi’ bin Khadij told me, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To Rafi’: Do you rent out your fields? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, we rent them for a quarter and for an inch of barley. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: “Do not do that. Plant it, lend it, or keep it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4532","Hisham bin Ammar told us, he said: Yahya, who is Ibn Hamza, told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Najashi, on the authority of Rafi’, He said: Zuhair bin Rafi’ came to us and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade something that was common among us. I said: What is that? What he said?” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, it is true. He said: He asked me: How do you produce in your fields? I said: We rent it for a quarter and an wasaq of dates? Or barley. He said: Do not do that. Plant it, sow it, or keep it."
"4533","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, he said: he told me Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Usayd bin Rafi’ bin Khadij, that Rafi’’s brother said to his people: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Peace and blessings of God be upon him today about something. He was kind to you and his command was obedience and goodness. He forbade the field. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4534","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hurmuz. He said: I heard Usayd ibn Rafi’ ibn Khadij al-Ansari mentioning, “They prohibited muhaqala, which is land that is cultivated on some of what is in it.”"
"4535","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Yazid Abi Shuja`, he said: He told me Issa bin Sahl bin Rafi’ bin Khadij said: “I am an orphan in the care of my grandfather Rafi’ bin Khadij, and I met a man and performed Hajj with him, so my brother came.” Imran bin Sahl bin Rafi bin Khadij, and he said: O my father, we have granted so-and-so land to us for two hundred dirhams, so he said: O my son, let That is because God Almighty will make for you a provision other than that. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has forbidden the leasing of land.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4536","Al-Hussein bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Muhammad, On the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, he said: Zaid bin Thabit said: May God forgive Rafi’ bin Khadij. I, by God, forgive him. I know the hadith from him, “It was just two men who fought, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If this is your affair, do not be averse to it.” Farms, then Rafi’ heard his saying: Do not invade the farms.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4537","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Muhammad bin Ammar, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Al-Walid, on the authority of Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Thabit, he said: By God, I am more knowledgeable about the hadith than Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, it only came Two men fought, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If this is your concern, then do not hate the farms.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4538","Isma'il ibn Mas'ud informed us, he said: Bashr narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu 'Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ammar, from al-Walid ibn al-Walid, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: \May Allah forgive Rafi' ibn Khadij—I was more knowledgeable about the hadith. Two men from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," having fought with one another. He said: 'If this is your state"," then do not lease out agricultural lands.' So his words were heard: 'Do not lease out agricultural lands.'\""\n\nAbu 'Abd al-Rahman said: A written sharecropping contract stipulating that the seed and expenses are borne by the landowner"," and the sharecropper receives one-quarter of what Allah"," the Mighty and Sublime"," produces from it—this is a document written by so-and-so son of so-and-so"," in sound health and with lawful authority"," for so-and-so son of so-and-so"," stating: \""You have handed over to me all of your land situated in such-and-such a place in such-and-such a city"," as a sharecropping arrangement. It is the land known as such-and-such"," bounded by four boundaries that encompass it entirely"," one of which adjoins such-and-such along its entire length"," and the second"," third"," and fourth likewise. You have handed over to me all of this land"," defined in this document by its surrounding boundaries"," along with all its rights"," its water supply"," its rivers"," and its irrigation channels—as an empty"," vacant plot of land"," containing neither trees nor crops—for a complete year"," the first of which is the beginning of such-and-such month in such-and-such year"," and the last of which is the end of such-and-such month in such-and-such year"," on the condition that I cultivate all of this land defined in this document"," whose location is described therein"," during this specified year"," from its beginning to its end"," with whatever I wish and see fit to plant of wheat"," barley"," sesame"," rice"," cotton"," fresh vegetables"," green beans"," chickpeas"," cowpeas"," lentils"," cucurbits"," melons"," carrots"," turnips"," radishes"," onions"," garlic"," herbs"," aromatic plants"," and all other produce"," winter and summer"," with your seeds and your planting material"," all of which is your responsibility and not mine; and that I undertake this with my own hand and with whomever I wish of my helpers"," my laborers"," my oxen"," and my tools; and that I attend to the cultivation and tending thereof"," and to whatever promotes its growth and proper maintenance"," including the ploughing of its land"," the clearing of its weeds"," the watering of whatever needs watering of what is planted"," the fertilizing of whatever needs fertilizing"," the digging of its irrigation channels and rivers"," the harvesting of whatever is to be harvested"," the gathering thereof"," the threshing of whatever is to be threshed"," and the winnowing thereof—all at your expense and not mine. I shall carry out all of this with my own hand and my helpers"," without your involvement. In return"," for all that Allah"," the Mighty and Sublime"," produces from all of the above during the period described in this document"," from its beginning to its end"," three-quarters shall be yours by virtue of your land"," your water supply"," your seed"," and your expenses"," and the remaining one-quarter shall be mine by virtue of my cultivation"," my labor"," and my tending of it with my own hand and my helpers. You have handed over to me all of this land defined in this document"," along with all its rights and appurtenances"," and I have taken possession of all of that from you on such-and-such a day"," in such-and-such a month"," in such-and-such a year. All of it has come into my possession"," and I have no ownership over any part of it"," nor any claim or demand"," except this sharecropping arrangement described in this document for the year specified therein. When that period expires"," all of it shall be returned to you and to your possession"," and you shall have the right to expel me from it after its expiration and to remove it from my possession and from the possession of anyone who has acquired any claim therein through me.\"" So-and-so and so-and-so have acknowledged this"," and this document has been written in two copies."""
"4539","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave to the Jews of Khaybar the palm trees of Khaybar and its land on the condition that they would work it from their own money, and that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, May God bless him and grant him peace, half of its fruit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4540","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us, saying: Shuaib ibn al-Layth told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd The Most Gracious, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He gave the Jews of Khaybar the palm trees of Khaybar and its land on the condition that They work it and cultivate it with their money, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, owns half of what comes out of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4541","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us, saying: Shuaib ibn al-Layth told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah bin Omar used to say: “Farms were rented during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the condition that “The Lord of the land has the crops in the waterer’s spring and a bunch of hay. I don’t know how much it is.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4542","Ali ibn Hajar informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, he said: “My two uncles used to farm For a third and a quarter, and their partner’s father, Alqamah, and Al-Aswad know, but they will not change it.”"
"4543","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Muammar, on the authority of Abdul-Karim Al-Jazari, he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr, Ibn Abbas said: “The best thing you can do is to rent out his land to one of you for gold and paper.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4544","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Ammar, Saad, and I participated on the day of Badr, and Saad brought two captives, but I and Ammar did not bring anything.”"
"4545","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: I am Habban, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: “ “If you hire a worker, tell him his wage.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4546","Amr bin Zurarah told us, he said: I am Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: I am Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: “A man came And a woman came to Ali, and a group of people was with each one of them. When he sent the detectives, he said: Take your time until I inform you of what is wrong with you. Do you know? What is the matter with you? If you think that you should come together, you should unite, and if you think that you should separate, you should separate. Then he went to the woman and said: You are satisfied. What was the ruling? She said: Yes, I am satisfied with the decree of God upon me as a guardian. Then he approached the man and said: Are you satisfied with what he decided? He said: No, but I am satisfied That they should be brought together and I do not want them to be separated. So Ali said: You lied, by God, you will not leave until you are satisfied with the same as I have been satisfied with.”"
"4547","It was read to Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad bin Shuaib bin Ali al-Nasa’i. Shuaib bin Yusuf and Muhammad bin al-Muthanna told you: Yahya told us: On the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, and Muhammad said in his hadith: I heard Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: “The worst of earnings are the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the earnings of a cupper.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4548","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Hatim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Evil Earnings are the dowry of a prostitute, the price of a dog, and the earnings of a cupper.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4549","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Jaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, On the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “The worst of earnings are the earnings of cuppers, the price of a dog, and a dowry.” The prostitute"
"4550","Ali bin Al-Mundhir Al-Kufi told us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah I heard Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The unlawful thing is three times the dowry of a prostitute, the earnings of a cupper, and the price of a \the dog\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4551","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Qattan told us, Abdul-Rahman bin Mughraa told us, Muhammad, who is Ibn Ishaq, told us, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among the unlawful things is the price of The dog, the dowry of the prostitute, and the cupper’s earnings.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It is similar to the fact that Ibn Fudayl traces Abd al-Rahman’s lineage to his grandfather. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4552","Hisham bin Ammar told us, Yahya told us, meaning bin Hamza, Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qariz, On the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A cupper’s earnings are evil, and the dowry of a transgressor is evil.” Wicked, and the price of a dog is wicked.”"
"4553","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Abdullah bin Hisham told me Ibrahim bin Qarith, that Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid narrated to him, that Rafi’ bin Khadij narrated to him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He earned A cupper is evil, the dowry of a prostitute is evil, and the price of a dog is evil.”"
"4554","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, who said: “Umar bin Al-Khattab, Abu Ka’b, ordered And Tamim al-Dari, to perform eleven rak'ahs for the people. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4555","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, he said: “ “I went to see Umm Salamah, and she told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in the morning in a state of ritual impurity without a wet dream, and then he would fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4556","She told us, along with this hadith, that she told him that she “brought a roasted lamb to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ate from it and then He stood up to pray, but did not perform ablution.”"
"4557","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Aliya and Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told us, saying: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Muhammad bin Yusuf told me, Ata’ bin Yassar told him that Umm Salamah told him, “She brought a roasted lamb to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ate from it.” Then he stood up to pray and did not perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4558","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, ate a shoulder of a sheep, but did not perform ablution."
"4559","Isma bin Al-Fadl Al-Naysaburi told me, Yahya bin Adam told me, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Humaid Al-Rawasi, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: “A man from Banu Al-Saqq, one of Banu Kilab, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and asked him about the stallion’s berries, but he forbade it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4560","Muhammad ibn Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he is a gendarme, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, I heard Ibn Abi Naam, I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the profit of a cupper, the price of a dog, or the price of a stallion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4561","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun told me, Muhammad, who is the son of Yusuf, told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, and Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: I Hibban, I am Abdullah and he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham Abi Kulayb, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: “It was forbidden “On the authority of the stallion” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4562","Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Habib told us, Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Abdullah bin Numayr, Asbat told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah. He said: Abu Hurairah said: “Four things that are unlawful are the killing of a stallion, the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the earnings of a cupper.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4563","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ told me that Sa’id, a client of Khalifa, told him: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The cupper’s tax, the price of a dog, and the dowry of the adulteress are unlawful matters.” Amr narrated it, on the authority of Ata’, and Sa’id said (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4564","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Sa`id, the servant of Khalifa, I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: “ “The price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the earnings of a cupper are unlawful.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4565","Wasil bin Abd al-Ala al-Kufi told us, Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, for the price of a dog and the herb of a goat."
"4566","Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told us, Ibn Abi Ubaidah told us, my father told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “The price of a dog and the dowry of a transgressor are not permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4567","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir say: “The Messenger forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, about striking a camel, and about selling water.”"
"4568","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of stallion’s honey.”"
"4569","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abd God said: “Ammar, I, and Sa’d joined forces on the day of Badr, and Sa’d brought two captives, but Ammar and I did not bring anything.”"
"4570","Abu Abdul Rahman Ahmad bin Shuaib told us, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us Amr, he said: Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “When God created Paradise and Hell, He sent Gabriel went to Paradise and said: Look at it and what I have prepared for its people therein. Then he looked at it and came back and said: By your might, no one will hear of it. No one entered it and ordered it to be surrounded by calamities. He said: Go to it and look at it and what I have prepared for its people therein. So he looked. Then, behold, it was surrounded by calamity. He said: By your glory, I feared that no one would enter it. He said: Go and look at the Fire. And what I have prepared for its people therein. He looked at it and saw that it was one over the other. Then he came back and said: By Your might, no one will enter it. So he ordered it to be surrounded by desires, so he said: Go back to it and look at it. So he looked at it, and behold, it was surrounded by desires, so he returned. He said: By Your glory, I feared that no one would escape from it unless he entered it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4571","Ahmad bin Sulaiman and Musa bin Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi reported, saying: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba. On the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: “It was an oath taken by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is the One who turns hearts.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4572","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Salt Abu Ya’la told us, he said: Abdullah bin Raja’ told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: “It was an oath from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, by which he swore no. And the one who transforms hearts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4573","Ali bin Hajar reported, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Abdullah bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever swears an oath, let him swear only by God, and the Quraysh used to swear by their fathers, so he said: Do not swear by your fathers.”"
"4574","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ibn Ulayya told me, he said: Yahya bin Abi Ishaq told me, he said: A man from Banu Ghaffar told me, in The meeting of Salem bin Abdullah, he said: Salem said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God He forbids you from swearing by your fathers.”"
"4575","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed and Qutayba bin Saeed reported and the wording for it, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, he said: “He heard The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Omar, and he said: “And my father and my father.” Then he said: “God forbids you from swearing by your fathers.” Omar said: “By God, what I swore by it afterward, whether remembering or not (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4576","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid and Sa`id bin Abdul Rahman reported, and the wording for it, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Omar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God forbids you from swearing by your fathers.” By God, I have not sworn by it yet. Remembering or not (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4577","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed Al-Homsi told me, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of His father told him, on the authority of Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God forbids you from swearing by your fathers.” Omar said: By God, I have never sworn by it yet, whether in memory or in retaliation. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4578","Abu Bakr bin Ali reported, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Muadh bin Muadh told us, saying: My father told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not swear by your fathers, nor by your mothers, nor by equals, and do not swear By God, unless you are truthful.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4579","Qutaibah bin Saeed narrated, saying: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ narrated, saying: Yazid narrated to us, he said: narrating to us Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is a liar.” It is as he said, and whoever kills himself for something, God will punish him for it in the fire of Hell.” And Qutaibah said in his hadith: with something intentionally. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4580","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr told us, on the authority of Yahya, that he told him, he said: Abu Amr told me, on the authority of Yahya, that he told me. Qalabah, he said: Thabit bin Al-Dahhak told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, is a liar. He said, “And whoever kills himself for something will be punished for it in the Hereafter.”"
"4581","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever says that I am free from Islam, then if he is lying, then he is as he said, and if he is truthful, he will not return to Islam.” “Islam is safe”"
"4582","Yusuf bin Issa Al-Maruzi reported, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, he said: Mis’ar reported, on the authority of Ma’abad bin Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yasar, on the authority of The murder of a woman from Juhayna, “A Jew came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: You denounce, and you associate, you say what God wills, and I will, and you say, “By the Kaaba.” So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded them, when they wanted to swear, to say: “By the Lord of the Kaaba.” And one of them says, “Whatever God wills, then I will.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4583","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Yazid told us, saying: Hisham reported, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Do not swear by your fathers or by the tyrants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4584","Kathir bin Ubaid reported, saying: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you swears an oath and says: By Al-Laat, let him say: There is no god but God, and whoever says to his companion, ‘Come.’” “I will gamble with you, so let him be honest.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4585","Abu Dawud Al-Harrani told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, and he is Ibn Ayan, trustworthy. He said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, On the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: “We were mentioning some matter while I was fresh from pre-Islamic times, so I swore by Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, so he said The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “What you said is miserable. Go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and tell him, for we will not see you unless we see you.” I disbelieved, so I met him and told him, and he said: Say: There is no god but Allah alone three times, and seek refuge from Satan three times, and avoid left three times and do not repeat it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4586","Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad narrated, saying: Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Musab bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of his father, he said: “ I swore by Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What an evil thing you said out of negligence, so I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I mentioned that to him, and he said: Say: There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. left for three days, and seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan, and then do not return.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4587","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Sulaym, trustworthy, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd. Ibn Muqrin, on the authority of Al-Baraa Ibn Aazib, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to do seven things: He commanded us to follow funerals, and to visit The sick, praising the one who sneezes, responding to the supplicant, supporting the oppressed, upholding the oath, and returning the greeting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4588","Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he is Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Zuhdam, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is not an oath on earth that I swear upon and see another that is better than it but I will fulfill it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4589","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad, who is Ibn Zayd, told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, he said: “ I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a group of Ash'arites whom we were carrying. He said: By God, I will not carry you, and I do not have anything. I will carry you. Then we stayed for as long as God wished, then camels were brought and he ordered us to have three animals. When we set off, we said to one another: He is not blessed. God is ours. We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to bear him. He swore he would not bear us, so we carried us. Abu Musa said: So we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted us, so we mentioned that to him, and he said: It was not me who carried you, but God carried you. Indeed, by God, God willing, I will not take an oath and see something else that is better. “Therefore, unless I atone for my oath and do what is better.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4590","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who “If he swore an oath and saw what was good, let him atone for his oath and do so.”"
"4591","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas told us, he said: Amr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears an oath and sees something else that is better than it, let him atone for his oath, and let that which is better come.”"
"4592","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Samurah, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If one of you takes an oath and sees something else that is better than it, let him atone for his oath, and look at what it is.” It is good, let him come to it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4593","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Samra told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “And when you take an oath, make amends for your oath and then do what is better.”"
"4594","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta’i al-Basri reported on the authority of Abd al-A’la, who is Ibn Abd al-A’la al-Basri, and mentioned a word that means it. Sa’id told us On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you take an oath and see something else... better than it, so make amends on your right hand and give that which is better.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4595","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abd al-Rahman reported, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr Mawla Al-Hasan bin Ali, narrating, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever takes an oath and sees something different better than it, so let the one who is better come and make atonement for his oath.”"
"4596","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfa, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever takes an oath and sees another oath that is better than it, let him abandon his oath and let the one that is better come.” And let him make her expiate.”"
"4597","Amr ibn Yazid reported, saying: Bahz ibn al-Asad told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi’ told me, saying: I heard Tamim bin Tarfat Al-Tai, narrating, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears an oath and sees good in it other than it, From it, let him come to the one who is best, and let him abandon his oath.”"
"4598","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: Abu al-Za’ra’ told us, on the authority of his uncle, Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of his father, he said: “I said: O Messenger of God, Have you seen a cousin of mine come to me and ask him, but he does not give me anything and does not reach me, then he needs me and comes to me and asks me, and I swore that I would neither give him nor Its origin, so he commanded me to go to what is best and make amends for my oath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4599","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour and Yunus reported, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you turn on an oath and see something else that is better, then go to the one that is better and atone for your oath.”"
"4600","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, he said: He said, meaning The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you take an oath and see something else better than it, then go to the one that is better and atone for your oath.”"
"4601","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Basri, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah said: He told me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you take an oath and see something else better than it, then go to the one that is better and atone for your oath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4602","Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Taymi reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin al-Akhnas, he said: Amr bin Shuaib told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No vow, no oath regarding what one does not have the right to do, no disobedience to God, no severing of family ties.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4603","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Khorasani told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever swears an oath and makes an exception, if he wishes he can make up for it, and if he wishes he may leave it without breaking his oath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4604","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sulayman bin Hayyan reported, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah bin Waqqas Al-Laythi, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Actions are but by intention, and a person is only what he intended. So whoever’s emigration is to God and His Messenger, his emigration is to God and to His Messenger, and whoever’s emigration is for a worldly gain or A woman he marries, and his migration is to where he migrated.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4605","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad reported, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, that Ata’ claimed that he heard Ubaid bin Umair saying: I heard Aisha claiming: “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stay with Zainab bint Jahsh and drink honey with her, so Hafsa and I agreed that Whichever of us the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has entered upon, let her say, “Indeed, I smell from you the scent of a Maghafir that has eaten a Maghafir.” So he entered upon one of them, and she said: That is for him, so he said: No, I drank honey with Zainab bint Jahsh, and I will not go back to it. So she descended: O Prophet, why do you forbid what God has made lawful for you? You seek the pleasure of your wives, if you repent to God for Aisha and Hafsa, and when the Prophet confided a hadith to some of his wives, saying: Rather, I drank honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4606","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Al-Muthanna bin Saeed told us, he said: Talha bin Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “I entered The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with his house, and when there was divorce and vinegar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat, how good the human being is.”"
"4607","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri Al-Basri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Qays. Ibn Abi Gharza said: “We were called brokers, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us while we were selling, and he gave us a name that was better for us than Our name, and he said: O merchants, this sale is attended by swearing and lying, so settle your sale with charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4608","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, Asim, and Jami’, on the authority of Abu Wa’il Shaqiq, on the authority of Qais bin Abu Gharza, he said: “We were selling in Al-Baqi’, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and we were called brokers, and he said: O community of merchants, So he called us by a name better than ours, and said: This sale is attended by backbiting and lying, so confuse it with charity. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4609","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Gharza, he said: “He came to us.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were in the market, said: This market is mixed with idle talk and lies, so tinge it with charity. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4610","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abi Wael, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Gharza, he said: “We were in the city selling We used to call ourselves brokers and the people called us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us one day. So he called us by a name that is better than the one we have given ourselves and the people have called us, and he said: O community of merchants, there is evidence that you are selling idle talk, so distort it. \With charity\"""""
"4611","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade vows, and said: It does not bring any good, but rather brings it out of \the miser\"""""
"4612","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade vows and said: It does not abolish anything, but rather extracts something from the stingy person.”"
"4613","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A vow does not advance or postpone anything, but rather it is something that can be extracted from what is stingy.”"
"4614","Abba Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The vow to the son of Adam is not something that He did not decree for him, but rather something that was extracted from the miser.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4615","Anba Qutayba bin Saeed said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Do not make a vow, for a vow does not take anything away from fate, but it only takes away from the miserly.”"
"4616","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Talha bin Abdul Malik, Thiqa, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever vows to obey God, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey God, let him not disobey Him.”"
"4617","Anba Amr bin Ali, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Malik told us, he said: Talha bin Abdul Malik told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever vows to obey God, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey God, let him not disobey Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4618","Anba Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ Al-Kufi said: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he is Ibn Omar bin Hafs bin Asim bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of Talha bin Abdul Malik, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever vows to obey... God, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey God, let him disobey Him.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Talha bin Abdul Malik, trustworthy, trustworthy, trustworthy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4619","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, whose name is Nasr bin Imran, on the authority of Zuhdam, he said : I heard Imran bin Husayn mention that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of you are my generation, then those after them, then those They follow them, then those who follow them.” I don’t know if he mentioned two centuries or three more. Then he mentioned a people who betray and do not trust, and bear witness. They will not be asked for martyrdom, nor will they make vows, nor will they fulfill them, and fatness will appear in them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4620","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Sulayman al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man leading a man on a horn, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached him and cut him off, saying: It is his vow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
